<title>SOUTH KOREA: Seoul court freezes assets of two Sammi units.</title>
<headline>Seoul court freezes assets of two Sammi units.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>A South Korean court has ordered frozen the assets of Sammi Steel Co and its sister firm, Sammi Corp, the two companies said on Monday in statements filed with the Korea Stock Exchange.  </p>
<p>On Tuesday the two core units of the Sammi Group filed for receivership with the Seoul District Court, seeking protection from their creditors.</p>
<p>The group is South Korea's 26th-largest conglomerate in terms of assets.</p>
<p>Sammi Steel is the nation's largest producer of specialty stainless steel products and Sammi Corp is a trading unit of the group.</p>
<p>The statements gave no more details.</p>
<p>-- Seoul newsroom (822) 727-5646</p>
</text>
